/// The updater (`updater`, 351-UPD-0007, docs/update/updater.md): turns a published release into a staged, verified
/// slot, and nothing more (MC-9.2–9.4, MC-3.11). It checks a channel's signature with the release key built into it,
/// a manifest's with the boot key, and every file it stages by size and SHA-256, before a boot record names the slot.
/// The parser service reads the metadata (MC-11.11). The source, the channel and what the updater does by itself are
/// in `update.txt` on the boot volume. A request runs to its end before the next one is read.
package mind:update@1.0.0;

interface update {
    /// Why a request failed. `no-source`: update.txt names no source; `no-slot`: the system did not boot from a slot;
    /// `trial`: the running slot is on trial, so the other one is its fallback and stays as it is; `network`: the
    /// source did not answer, or a transfer failed after its tries; `missing`: the source has no such file, or the
    /// channel no manifest for this architecture; `malformed`: the parser refused the metadata, or its answer does not
    /// make the bytes; `signature`: a channel or manifest not signed by its key; `expired`: the channel's expiry has
    /// passed, or the clock cannot be read; `older`: the channel names the running version or an older one; `digest`:
    /// a file not as its manifest lists it; `write`: the slot or a boot record could not be written; `not-staged`: no
    /// verified newer release in the other slot; `no-fallback`: no slot to roll back to, or its version is not known or
    /// is below the minimum; `denied`: init refused the restart; `no-parser`: the parser service did not answer.
    enum error { no-source, no-slot, trial, network, missing, malformed, signature, expired, older, digest, write, not-staged, no-fallback, denied, no-parser }

    /// What a channel offers: its name, latest version, minimum and expiry, and the running version (0: not known).
    record offer { channel: string<32>, version: u64, minimum: u64, expires: string<20>, running: u64 }

    /// The updater's view: the running slot (`A`, `B`, or 0 when the system booted from the volume's root), whether it
    /// runs on trial, its version (0: not known); the slot the newer boot record names (0: none) and whether that
    /// record is confirmed; the version staged in the other slot (0: none); the last failure (empty: none).
    record state { slot: u8, trial: bool, running: u64, recorded: u8, confirmed: bool, staged: u64, failure: string<64> }

    /// Reads the channel and checks its signature, its form and its expiry. A version not above the running one is
    /// `older`.
    check: func() -> result<offer, error>;
    /// Checks, then stages the newer release in the other slot: every boot file its manifest lists, resumed where a
    /// partial file ends and checked by size and SHA-256, then the manifest, its signature and the channel. Returns the
    /// version staged.
    fetch: func() -> result<u64, error>;
    /// Checks the other slot as the bootloader will, writes the boot record that boots it on trial with `tries` (1 to
    /// 9), falling back to the running slot, and asks init to restart the machine.
    apply: func(tries: u8) -> result<_, error>;
    /// Writes the boot record that boots the other slot on trial, falling back to the running one, if the channel kept
    /// there shows a version not below the minimum the updater knows; then asks init to restart the machine.
    rollback: func() -> result<_, error>;
    /// The updater's view (above).
    status: func() -> state;
}
